    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F14. K-invariance (Tier 2, Lindblad scaling) @ HEAD:785","c769952cd6a1d011b202774e7123f53a9c838696368cc7f1a1fd6614b403e910","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","### F14. K-invariance (Tier 2, Lindblad scaling)"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F14. K-invariance (Tier 2, Lindblad scaling) @ HEAD:787","5e78871826da0d0a2aca0e0b817f77ba1a66cf9e8839ca00b8eef719b5180f58","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","    K = gamma * t_cross = constant per bridge type"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F14. K-invariance (Tier 2, Lindblad scaling) @ HEAD:802","506187c8d2df07d8e9b425b036b2fac753d8a74003248e1138b720752e9269e5","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","Standard Lindblad time-rescaling (τ = γt), not deep physics."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F14. K-invariance (Tier 2, Lindblad scaling) @ HEAD:806","7b077688316928ec079274e12ac81cd987ed0361918c3dfe5d6c95395b3396a0","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","reaches K-invariance through \"all observables depend on τ = γt\", and that step"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F14. K-invariance (Tier 2, Lindblad scaling) @ HEAD:830","0eac73eac5d54662d65e01c7c3d19c8c42e3c46a0031abd0e8305a16e6e17ca3","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","γ is read as external illumination and `K=γt` as exposure. The invariance in"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F14. K-invariance (Tier 2, Lindblad scaling) @ HEAD:835","16faad0ec0f6465a1aa90b1d9eb61fd9d9a7dd863034726138d828c376f5142c","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","factor. Multiplying by time makes `K=γt` dimensionless, but the theorem does"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F25. CΨ closed form, Bell+ Z-dephasing (Tier 1, proven) @ HEAD:884","b603a75b7634cc4bcc6f07c45aec31621f8c69626c23e944734c293813454cf6","F25","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F25","    CPsi(t) = f * (1 + f^2) / 6,       f = e^{-4*gamma*t}"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F25. CΨ closed form, Bell+ Z-dephasing (Tier 1, proven) @ HEAD:889","51be8633c317ab54c112a3d78153484317cff33a6efc54fca8104de8a65c7ede","F25","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F25","K = gamma * t_cross = 0.0374."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F27. K values per noise channel (Tier 1, from F26) @ HEAD:931","cfd8b1235de7d7ffe6bd83db06df8481b7ecf3f37c94a2233507662718c6b9fb","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","Complements F14 (K per bridge metric). These are K per"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F27. K values per noise channel (Tier 1, from F26) @ HEAD:944","9908c88a6d2be68311894fe8b9ed6bb87c54952610138b43fb05fc430b68e0e1","F26","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F26","conserved. With the norm pinned, the surviving decay is v = e^{−4γt} and"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F31. Relay protocol MI bound (Tier 2, N=11) @ HEAD:1204","3d455e9ae06c3c95ebddd8b9ca1f75b514ca19d0955b43021d89f0b126dfec79","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","Six relay stages, each t_stage = K/gamma. Receiving qubits get"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F31. Relay protocol MI bound (Tier 2, N=11) @ HEAD:1206","1978d72a91d917cee51d8cab7620fd5edcc7a2f4dc510e109a8fa80d7df2635f","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","results: K/gamma timing (F14), quiet receiver (F29),"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F55. Absorption dose K_death (Tier 1 above Q*_gap(N), from D6) @ HEAD:1764","bb865bf22c5f47d01aafbadc10bc79fdfbd3dfdf216303ac8568f1719c3b4391","F55","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F55","K_fold is the dose K = gamma*t at which CPsi crosses 1/4, read off the F25"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F55. Absorption dose K_death (Tier 1 above Q*_gap(N), from D6) @ HEAD:1777","d77b11b25b4ba21ffbb0a7bdae506e07583a1eae24e3205b84aaf01b2494ac2c","D6/F55","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:D6/F55","K = γ · t = ln(100)/2 = ln(10) = 2.303. Independent of N, γ, topology."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F57. Trajectory dwell time at CΨ = 1/4 (Tier 1, analytical) @ HEAD:1851","a7708199c95a98ca99b52ac75d19a95f555a6b1231543822d74d5f8ce817bcf2","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","universal gamma-invariance or isolation of the discrepancy's cause. Both"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F65. Single-excitation spectrum of uniform open XX chain (Tier 1, proven, verified N=3..30) @ HEAD:2127","d6b6098b2cd2da2eddc8f5695a65dd9f171a61487e5c8a32091843be91d3ca04","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","    α_k / γ₀ = (4 / (N+1)) · sin²(kπ / (N+1)),    k = 1, ..., N"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F65. Single-excitation spectrum of uniform open XX chain (Tier 1, proven, verified N=3..30) @ HEAD:2129","3be06102adf78602066fc7c619a51c1dd74c7f1507c228378bd04289ca1476f9","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","This is F64 evaluated on the analytically known eigenvectors ψ_k(i) = √(2/(N+1)) · sin(πk(i+1)/(N+1)) of the N×N tridiagonal single-excitation Hamiltonian. The endpoint amplitude |ψ_k(N-1)|² = (2/(N+1)) · sin²(kπ/(N+1)), and the Absorption Theorem gives α_k = 2γ₀ · |a_B|²."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F65. Single-excitation spectrum of uniform open XX chain (Tier 1, proven, verified N=3..30) @ HEAD:2136","66da838e976eb476f6f52d6c4e385bd87cca253ef2f0aef77ac049509fa7c3f6","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","**Niven rationality.** All α_k/γ₀ are rational if and only if N+1 ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4, 6}, i.e., N ∈ {0, 1, 2, 3, 5}. For all other N the values are algebraic irrationals (golden-ratio family at N=4,9; √2 family at N=7; general cyclotomic otherwise). This follows from Niven's theorem applied to α_k/γ₀ = (2/(N+1))·(1 − cos(2kπ/(N+1))):"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F65. Single-excitation spectrum of uniform open XX chain (Tier 1, proven, verified N=3..30) @ HEAD:2153","c2db216df0f9bcc8eaadc4edf95333544267a0fdadd9111eda6ce998b6cbef8e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","    dE_k/du |_{u=0} = 2·ψ_k(0)·ψ_k(N−1) = (−1)^{k+1} · α_k/γ₀        (units of J),"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F67. Bonding-mode encoding is the optimal dephasing-protected Bell pair (Tier 1, verified N=3, N=5) @ HEAD:2193","5b055d2dbcd8ff11558b3f128ad886471683ffee3b61431d4936249e804335b5","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","with |ψ_1⟩ = √(2/(N+1)) · Σᵢ sin(π(i+1)/(N+1)) |1ᵢ⟩ (the k=1 bonding mode of F65) decays as a pure exponential from t=0:"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F75. Mirror-pair MI for single-excitation mirror-symmetric states (Tier 1, proven algebraic) @ HEAD:2547","a76756233312c9a45bbd8cdbc93c03ea08d86fff853c5c9cca74622f42a7d452","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","Under Heisenberg evolution on the uniform chain, bonding mode ψ_k mixes with its same-parity partner ψ_{N+1−k} via the boundary ZZ term. At N = 5 for bonding:2 the partner is ψ_4 which has identical mirror-pair populations p_ℓ (because sin²(πk(ℓ+1)/(N+1)) = sin²(π(N+1−k)(ℓ+1)/(N+1))); direct numerical propagation shows that MM(t) oscillates with period 2π/Δ (Δ = same-parity eigenvalue gap of the 2×2 block, Δ = 2√5 for N = 5) between a minimum near t = π/(2Δ) and a revival near t = π/Δ. Under uniform Z-dephasing at γ₀, the revival is damped but stays close to MM(0); the simulation-observed PeakMM matches MM(0) within 1% at N = 5 k = 2 (analytic 1.2451, numerical Lindblad max 1.2475 at t = 0.645, C# brecher PeakMM 1.2410 on a coarser grid). At larger N and different k the ratio drops to ~0.93 because the oscillation revival magnitude and dephasing decay combine less favourably."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F86. Q_peak chromaticity-specific N-invariant constants (Sammelbecken with three theorems) @ HEAD:3040","4536f7767f02292ff272f99560125907e68bc577719281c75ee75f64fa26fb00","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","- **F86a. EP mechanism** \\[Tier 1 derived\\]: Q_EP = 2/g_eff, t_peak = 1/(4γ₀); 2-level rate-channel exceptional point."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","#### F86a. EP mechanism: Q_EP = 2/g_eff, t_peak = 1/(4γ₀) \\[Tier 1 derived\\] @ HEAD:3101","f56024b678fc41f252bf4b20f49c9a9507156c29782cffb149e21a3009c81e5d","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","#### F86a. EP mechanism: Q_EP = 2/g_eff, t_peak = 1/(4γ₀) \\[Tier 1 derived\\]"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","#### F86a. EP mechanism: Q_EP = 2/g_eff, t_peak = 1/(4γ₀) \\[Tier 1 derived\\] @ HEAD:3113","68d323fc584d92b72b1f51a29ef4857d6e5a056d3dcd2a0a7caf223b28713995","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","    t_peak = 1 / (4γ₀)"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","#### F86c. F71 spatial-mirror invariance of per-bond Q_peak \\[Tier 1 derived\\] @ HEAD:3192","82ca983f2d81ca9920b633428766f91f059045df45faa11d70a55b3c2ed85b86","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","**Connection to PTF.** The same machinery that produces PTF's per-site α_i closure law (bilinear J-perturbation observables, eigenvector mixing under V_L) produces Q_peak at the (n, n+1)-block level. PTF's per-site is the c=1 (vac-SE) instance; F86's c ≥ 2 cases are the natural higher-chromaticity siblings. t_peak = 1/(4γ₀) is the EP time-scale universal to all c, one (n, n+1)-block analogue of PTF's α-fitting time window."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F94. Born deviation dominant-outcome coefficient: |0+0+⟩ N=4 Heisenberg + Z-deph (Tier 1 derived, Dyson sym3 = 8 bit-exact; 2026-05-16) @ HEAD:3553","b378478ea987fa9b16021f0cb2a75b0ed8ee619987caf0d3b2a559aad0a78643","F94","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F94","    where Q = J/γ, K = γt, Δ_|00⟩ = P_lindblad(|00⟩) / P_unitary(|00⟩) − 1"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F94. Born deviation dominant-outcome coefficient: |0+0+⟩ N=4 Heisenberg + Z-deph (Tier 1 derived, Dyson sym3 = 8 bit-exact; 2026-05-16) @ HEAD:3571","ac17300aca9c67e0350da6beb26149450c06d2a5240753e1f9657f521dd75eff","F94","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F94","**Born-rule generalization context:** this is the first Tier-1 closed form for a per-outcome Born deviation under the framework's Q-K-invariant convention (Universal Carrier). Generalizes BORN_RULE_MIRROR's R_i = C_i · Ψ_i² (Tier 2/3, Feb 2026) to a specific case with explicit C_i closed form. The Δ_i values for other outcomes of the same setup scale linearly in K (1st-order diagrams) rather than as Q²·K³; their coefficients are separately Tier-1-derivable via the same Dyson method."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F96. Born deviation subdominant-outcome slopes: |0+0+⟩ N=4 Heisenberg + Z-deph, pair (0,2) (Tier 1 derived, bit-exact Dyson + unitary matrix elements; 2026-05-17) @ HEAD:3640","49536b2ef3ce6c5f836e32e191be2087fa6884f6a5288b86b597027d1ab1a19f","F96","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F96","with K = γt the Universal-Carrier observable."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F96. Born deviation subdominant-outcome slopes: |0+0+⟩ N=4 Heisenberg + Z-deph, pair (0,2) (Tier 1 derived, bit-exact Dyson + unitary matrix elements; 2026-05-17) @ HEAD:3657","7394d66a3caeea3351f60bed03896fedb9efa14253213dadca0a701dda9f5eae","F96","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F96","where M_n^{(i)} = ⟨i|_pair Tr_{1,3}[sym_n^1 · ρ_0]|i⟩_pair and U_{2k}^{(i)} = ⟨i|_pair Tr_{1,3}[L_h^{2k} · ρ_0]|i⟩_pair (h := H/J). The J^{2k} factors cancel automatically → Q-independence; only γt = K survives."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F101. F71 c₁ bond-mirror deviation is exactly odd in the F71-anti-palindromic γ (observable-side twin of F91) (Tier 1 derived, algebraic + numerically verified N=3,4,5; 2026-05-21) @ HEAD:3957","aa89c25a9bca3fb1f1d0dbe5cce5a2c84f39206bbf61ffcf2ef985f1a81f9b86","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","**Connection to F91:** observable-side twin of F91. F91 (spectrum side) = the F71-refined diagonal-block eigenvalue multiset depends only on γ_sym (the pair-sums S_l = γ_l + γ_{N−1−l} = 2·γ_sym[l]; γ_anti invisible to the spectrum). F101 (observable side) = the c₁ bond-mirror deviation vanishes for palindromic γ and is exactly odd in γ_anti; its parity and zero set are fixed by γ_anti alone, while its magnitude κ_γ also depends on γ_sym (above). Two faces of one γ_sym/γ_anti split. The J-side observable twin is F100."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F101. F71 c₁ bond-mirror deviation is exactly odd in the F71-anti-palindromic γ (observable-side twin of F91) (Tier 1 derived, algebraic + numerically verified N=3,4,5; 2026-05-21) @ HEAD:3959","16a2874abd918a6c4a9f636846c9b8502bbc6aebe3e9a3647e9a150d4f8ebd86","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","**Scope:** c₁ only. The F86c per-bond Q_peak observable is not covered: its Q-axis Q = J/γ₀ and EP time t_peak = 1/(4γ₀) are defined against a scalar γ₀, which a non-uniform per-site γ does not provide. The γ_avg-anchored Q_peak route and the h-detuning observable twin follow by the same parameter-agnostic argument and are noted in PROOF_F101 as separable extensions."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F108 Part 1. Π²-Even Hamiltonians Always Admit an Exact Palindrome Operator (Tier 1 derived, Π_5bilinear phase variant of canonical P1 Π) @ HEAD:4292","85540717c338df82a45e50e3f02705994801a0b0219c45126d147acef05671bb","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","(BitA axis, bit_a=0 bilinears):"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F120. The moment-tower pump channel: the device's own damping reads the girth ladder linearly (Tier 1 derived; structural law confirmed on ibm_kingston 2026-06-11) @ HEAD:5163","6cba1dd1cb62dc2d513c71f3a402db5162712af142f17e4d289354fb5d77da5f","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","has ℓ = 0 and k = 2, yet p₅ = 7680γ is a positive monomial and m\\* = 5 = 2k+1 exactly)."],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F126. The dephasing front renewal: the walk in the light is the wave, caught and released (representation + Green's function Tier 1 exact; the survival readings Tier 1 candidate; 2026-07-13) @ HEAD:5481","7b3a5b2c1f6b822cad45aadb6fdac6abdf81f8841e78de39ec98acfba60516ff","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","  **P_n(t) = e^{−Γt}·S_n(t),  S_n(t) = |G_{n0}(t)|² + Γ·∫₀ᵗ ds Σ_m |G_{nm}(t−s)|²·S_m(s)**"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F126. The dephasing front renewal: the walk in the light is the wave, caught and released (representation + Green's function Tier 1 exact; the survival readings Tier 1 candidate; 2026-07-13) @ HEAD:5489","4b584d303569a70534604be841897a0165266d7696b76b8e1c359bc7bf6fb59b","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","cleanly between catches; every refill order carries the same universal `e^{−Γt}`, the `j = 0` term is"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F134. The two-row reflection law of the F133 coefficients: along any fixed second row, the table is a palindrome (verified exactly over ℤ 2026-07-17; minted 2026-07-17) @ HEAD:6038","da0d3293ff8e4b31d6a6cdc8f8941ce6fa5f67e6cfe73bd5b08e7d6d51d0663f","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","beyond-wall shadow, with Θ_k = (t²²−t⁻²²)·P_k explicit (P₀ = −(C₁₀+C₆),"],
    ["docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md","### F160. The cracked ring is exactly solvable: with one bond of the XY ring detuned to u·J, u = J′/J, and E = 2J·cos k, for u < 1 the whole single-excitation spectrum is the zero set on the open interval (0, π) of G(k) = (1 − u²)·sin(Nk)·cos k + [(1 + u²)·cos(Nk) − 2u]·sin k = sin((N+1)k) − u²·sin((N−1)k) − 2u·sin k, multiplicities included, because det(2J·cos k·I − H) = J^N·G(k)/sin k (at u = 1 the band-edge levels sit at k = 0 and, for even N, k = π, where G vanishes for free; past u = 1 the departed levels ride the same curve continued to complex k); u is a boundary-condition parameter whose two ends are the two combs (u = 1 the ring's 2πm/N, u = 0 the open chain's πm/(N+1), F2b), the condition is the walk-time step's transmission amplitude closed into a loop, Re[e^(−iNk)/t(k)] = 1, the flat split 4δJ/N, δ = 1 − u, gets its next order ΔE_m = (4δJ/N)[1 + δ(½ − 1/(N·sin²k_m)) + O(δ²)], and past u = 1 how many levels leave the band is a parity law (Tier 1: derived and gated 2026-08-31 in THE_CRACKED_BELL §The crack is exactly solvable and stated the same day in the sibling COUPLING_DEFECT_WALK_TIME_STEP, both committed 2026-09-01 in 20bc844; registered 2026-09-01 as an INDEX of those two pages, adding only one-line consequences: the polynomial clothing of the identity, its band-edge factor forms, the N = 4 Perron series and the Weyl bound that caps the departures at one per side) @ HEAD:9022","7eeeff446d1b2b9229c45f76ccad8e982a4dfe7c14db7759b828bfe4793f403e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","409b84e686b2edb7d69b4dda05bc83bb1983dce22db67b6c778c11f0d1425665","chain-end velocity dE_k/du = (−1)^{k+1}·α_k/γ₀, F65's endpoint rates signed, from the"],
    ["docs/GAMMA_TIME_DISTINCTION.md","# Gamma Sets a Dissipative Scale; It Does Not Define Time @ HEAD:4","90abfb7d0392cb5adc6a90ab107774ef5ec3dc3ee31f117db1bef957e03c351d","F14/mixed","CONTROL","CONTROL:90abfb7d0392cb5adc6a90ab107774ef5ec3dc3ee31f117db1bef957e03c351d","comparison, tau gamma t scaling, no experienced-time ontology -->"],
    ["docs/GAMMA_TIME_DISTINCTION.md","## The tau collapse, and what it actually measures @ HEAD:50","b6ba30fb877f603571d68be776e4e61a7da82474edce3d06d1381d8c69d69ea4","F14/mixed","CONTROL","CONTROL:b6ba30fb877f603571d68be776e4e61a7da82474edce3d06d1381d8c69d69ea4","`tau = gamma*t`. So every observable is a function of `tau` **and** of"],
    ["docs/GAMMA_TIME_DISTINCTION.md","## The tau collapse, and what it actually measures @ HEAD:77","895e7423e0c0a7427eaa7ebe12f3849e9dd90525bb55e8b9317920940667849e","F14/mixed","CONTROL","CONTROL:895e7423e0c0a7427eaa7ebe12f3849e9dd90525bb55e8b9317920940667849e","`tau = gamma*t` **is** this generator's own time. At fixed `J` they do not, and"],
    ["docs/GAMMA_TIME_DISTINCTION.md","## Precise language @ HEAD:104","f9bdc449fea34e712faf02baad64b298c82097831b4d597ff742ecab7cbe90fc","F14/mixed","CONTROL","CONTROL:f9bdc449fea34e712faf02baad64b298c82097831b4d597ff742ecab7cbe90fc","| `tau = gamma*t` alone determines the trajectory at fixed J | False; measured to fail on all four observables above |"],
