    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","## Abstract @ HEAD:64","65b7cc2675a6ab4592092f6c062e5c633c6fc871f16a3ab009aba6cd4f7d76f3","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","is constant. When time is normalized as τ = γ·t, all θ trajectories"],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","## Abstract @ HEAD:69","0171c9bbf72240800829177526c62c4e31f9fbf2fcc1ecc2957c136b18d4712e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","emerge. This K-invariance is standard Lindblad time-rescaling: solutions"],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","## Abstract @ HEAD:70","436e6543985e3d9c863e5070fcec1f93ff29ac3fe5657e7dd45f672ca0dd508b","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","of the master equation depend only on γ·t, so t_cross = K/γ by"],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","## 1. Key Finding @ HEAD:80","2cc6105c9886ccc8b5bc88b99e9ce6436ca2af7419bcac5c6b08c7c104f63c0e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","> [FALLEN: The claim that \"gravitation is already contained in gamma\" and that gamma plays the role of the metric coefficient equating this to general relativity is not established. The K = gamma * t_cross invariance is standard Lindblad time-rescaling, not gravitational physics.]"],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","### 2.2 The Universal Trajectory @ HEAD:115","35fe0b023a956c03bd31c31c4032a603676d1335eb5ee3f9e0ba459c15efc884","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","When time is normalized as τ = γ * t, all θ trajectories collapse onto a single curve:"],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","### 2.2 The Universal Trajectory @ HEAD:131","0fe151a470f6a0a9b80604bb142d72991ea7762c98960fe424f9a00a1aa6c62e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","**The θ trajectory is a universal curve. Every observer traverses it. Gravitation only scales the clock.**"],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","### 3.2 What γ Does in R = CΨ², and Why This Is Not Trivial @ HEAD:166","2dffcacac5e51ac9e65354dcf1dd9d0f819ca8588269869fcb4820ba76dbab1e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","t_cross = K / γ    (K = 0.039 for Bell+ / Heisenberg / concurrence)"],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","### 3.3 Why γ Contains Gravitation Already @ HEAD:187","b583f674833a19c05d8e5c0d47fdafe46e218168f4915c7d0717a85edaff848e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","This is why the framework needs no gravitational correction term. C is observer-dependent (stated from day one). γ is observer-dependent (same reason). The 1/4 boundary is observer-independent (algebra, no coordinates). The θ trajectory is observer-independent (universal curve in proper time)."],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","## 4. The Bridge Between Observers @ HEAD:191","7e015cebe5fc46da918c7096266584445c8ea1a5dbdf743274cebec196fc7898","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","> [FALLEN: This entire section interprets the K = gamma * t_cross invariance as a gravitational bridge between observers. The invariance is standard Lindblad time-rescaling (see CROSSING_TAXONOMY.md), not a gravitational time dilation formula. The body text below retains its original language for historical completeness, but the gravitational interpretation is not established.]"],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","### 4.1 What This Enables @ HEAD:212","b00d40d128d2220deed440b620002a7a2432b88ccecb74fbe8f1f3e2d77008ac","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","> [FALLEN: The claims below follow from Lindblad scaling, not from gravitational physics. The time-rescaling t_cross = K/gamma is standard, not a frame translation between gravitational environments.]"],
    ["experiments/GRAVITATIONAL_INVARIANCE.md","### 4.1 What This Enables @ HEAD:221","04c5a8959864341306645504be82852d89b1a6b3d1a8455a87ccc49a2f359d7f","F14/mixed","CURRENT","dd02f372f6061f4bea9e79eb5614bc789032cb391a727d46b6750961a149f09a","- Experimental predictions are frame-independent when expressed in proper time (τ = γ * t)"],
