    ["experiments/METRIC_DISCRIMINATION.md","## What this document is about @ HEAD:35","54f05d7565cd6e464b4afe2249c5cf6570a7c1f9146922f7c82b69b45b48e52a","F14/mixed","CURRENT","493e59c234105371c5f17774bfe37b490ae27b5f936f808364a55ab701494d53","is the Lindblad scaling symmetry τ = γ·t."],
    ["experiments/METRIC_DISCRIMINATION.md","## Abstract @ HEAD:44","21a8edf15b03a0360f2dffa8dc2d7f36ca173e5179246e1497dd5182b763b809","F14/mixed","CURRENT","493e59c234105371c5f17774bfe37b490ae27b5f936f808364a55ab701494d53","exact standard-Lindblad K = ln(4/3)/8 = 0.03596, see the reproducibility note in §3.1). This K-invariance is a mathematical identity"],
