    ["experiments/METRIC_DISCRIMINATION.md","### 3.1 The Invariant @ HEAD:107","2e76eee035f74aa81f4c708c3ada1a27d3a828cd6ced7c9f13ee2d8d267bb0d5","F14/mixed","CURRENT","493e59c234105371c5f17774bfe37b490ae27b5f936f808364a55ab701494d53","value is K = 0.03596 (t = 0.719). The K-INVARIANCE result of this"],
    ["experiments/METRIC_DISCRIMINATION.md","### 4.1 Why Discrimination Fails @ HEAD:141","66ed2c7cd24dc74dc90e83ca4c31ddba82eb6f7230eaf0799a249c83a7eb6280","F14/mixed","CURRENT","493e59c234105371c5f17774bfe37b490ae27b5f936f808364a55ab701494d53","If γ is constant, the solution depends only on the product γ * t. This means t_cross = K / γ is a **mathematical identity**, not a physical constraint."],
    ["experiments/METRIC_DISCRIMINATION.md","### 6.3 Hamiltonian Dependence (Non-Eigenstate Regime) @ HEAD:238","908231189f23dab73e9fdccf266e4e79ab0f4977faa393c5da11df33329dce1e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","493e59c234105371c5f17774bfe37b490ae27b5f936f808364a55ab701494d53","**Implication**: K = γ * t_cross is well-defined only for monotonic C·Ψ trajectories. When the Hamiltonian drives the system, the \"first crossing\" time depends on the Hamiltonian frequency, not just γ. This does not invalidate the invariance; it means the invariance applies to the decoherence envelope, not the oscillatory dynamics."],
    ["experiments/METRIC_DISCRIMINATION.md","## 7. Summary @ HEAD:254","c127a210912396e33b66e475eeabb8b8f9ad81abcac1fb5bad2f8958962bf82a","F14/mixed","CURRENT","493e59c234105371c5f17774bfe37b490ae27b5f936f808364a55ab701494d53","**UPDATE 2026-02-18**: K-invariance has been extended to all three crossing bridges (concurrence K=0.039, mutual_info K=0.033, correlation K=0.072; all three are the February tool's feedback-model readings, the standard-Lindblad values being 0.03596 / 0.02966 / 0.07192). More importantly, K-invariance is now understood as a consequence of Lindblad scaling symmetry τ = γ·t, not a specific property of the ¼ boundary. See [Crossing Taxonomy](CROSSING_TAXONOMY.md)."],
    ["experiments/MINIMUM_CROSSING_ENERGY.md","## 4. The Three Regimes @ HEAD:156","137a0933e386835192b955cc85cdec9ca53202969feb27c3fa783161b6854dd0","F14/mixed","CURRENT","e20de1e0d78566a552f524d6edfeae6662f51559214cab814dd5b62562d82759","Crossing always occurs. Time scale: t_cross = K/γ."],
