    ["experiments/README.md","### The Lattice Thread (bridged worlds, dead sets, the opening law) @ HEAD:284","c8b61d5b45f9547ae4606bbc4b21267bfb18b78c2ad9fb35d63363d17494073d","F14/mixed","CURRENT","0b175a3cda7adfe106a9c33b1ee31ee86da37e3c250a040b1535432735dc46a7","| [The Motion and the Missing Phase](THE_MOTION_AND_THE_MISSING_PHASE.md) | Exploration note: light on the centre seat of an odd chain leaves the reflection-odd motion (F157) and its X^N copy untouched while the phase between the copies fades at e^(−2γt), unseen by every page below N−2 sites (F70) yet a real entanglement loss; a CNOT decoder brings it onto the centre, and the cross-copy block is the Lattice's one-sided reading X^N ρ as a block of a state. With an end defect (XY, N = 7) one parity-forced blind vector survives and the decoded distance plateaus at 0.763 / 0.734. Short-time onsets live-witnessed in exact ℚ(i) (`inspect --root missingphase`) |"],
    ["experiments/README.md","### F-Registry Readings (F64 through F130) @ HEAD:303","1a65f7ff6f9016146d73dd83161f26d49174d3378a39a17b70cc498d0c853883","F14/mixed","CURRENT","0b175a3cda7adfe106a9c33b1ee31ee86da37e3c250a040b1535432735dc46a7","| [F64 Topology Generalization](F64_TOPOLOGY_GENERALIZATION.md) | Tier 1: F64's cavity-mode-exposure rate α_k = 2γ_B·\\|a_B(ψ_k)\\|² generalizes to chain, star, ring, complete and Y-tree at N=5 and N=7, max relative error < 0.001 in the first-order regime |"],
