    ["hypotheses/GRAVITY_FROM_WAVE_DEATH.md","### Link 4: The sacrifice zone crosses 1/4 first @ HEAD:91","c9cc244f5b4c30f59a2905c442ff1d480aa1578f5cf94ba67f2cfa87361fc077","F14/mixed","CURRENT","86922a56f75c338aa624c452da2b89d705eb363fcdca699d9a99abf390ccc239","decoherence → earlier CΨ = 1/4 crossing. By [F14 K-invariance](../docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md), the crossing time scales as K = γ · t_cross. For Z-dephasing on Bell+ the closed form gives K = 0.0374 (F25); K depends on the noise channel (K_Z = 0.0374, K_X = K_Y = ln(2)/8 = 0.0866433…, K_depol = 0.0440)."],
    ["hypotheses/GRAVITY_FROM_WAVE_DEATH.md","### Link 4: The sacrifice zone crosses 1/4 first @ HEAD:97","c6a320a05f4fef90872f63bae9dc53a62b906b13b2addccd8a0822a6f2f21c8f","F14/mixed","CURRENT","86922a56f75c338aa624c452da2b89d705eb363fcdca699d9a99abf390ccc239","Source: [Resonant Return](../experiments/RESONANT_RETURN.md), [Receiver vs Gamma Sacrifice](../experiments/RECEIVER_VS_GAMMA_SACRIFICE.md), [Analytical Formulas](../docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md) (F14, F25), [Zero Is the Mirror](ZERO_IS_THE_MIRROR.md)."],
    ["hypotheses/PAIR_BREAKING_AT_THE_HORIZON.md","# The Pair Holds, the Fates Split: Decoherence as Hawking Radiation in Operator Space @ HEAD:23","964dd12e0ecd3caf24020e112ac0eacc286f88c7ff6f990ea7ea54db61faaf36","F14/mixed","CONTROL","CONTROL:964dd12e0ecd3caf24020e112ac0eacc286f88c7ff6f990ea7ea54db61faaf36","- [Analytical Formulas](../docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md) (K-invariance F14, Tier 2, and its 2026-08-29 scope note: the Lindblad scaling symmetry is joint, so the invariance belongs to the Hamiltonian-blind Bell⁺ sector rather than to any Lindblad system)"],
    ["hypotheses/PAIR_BREAKING_AT_THE_HORIZON.md","## The isomorphism @ HEAD:199","a9a5ff46de4a32427b4276b9da0f46341e21ebd27c7af9d8cba12a54462e7852","F14/mixed","CONTROL","CONTROL:a9a5ff46de4a32427b4276b9da0f46341e21ebd27c7af9d8cba12a54462e7852","| Spacetime interval c × τ = invariant | [K-invariance](../docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md) γ × t = const (F14), in the Bell⁺ sector only | 2 |"],
    ["hypotheses/PERSPECTIVAL_TIME_FIELD.md","# The Perspectival Time Field @ HEAD:10","da869f4a27b0120580eff0e484bf6c2628647a80b47a684d46a27d30febacc2e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","9cfa7c1d80bd56c5f4f18042a6163ebd159f6117d70e940df5fd914ab50a9b19","[Analytical Formulas](../docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md) (F4, F14, F65),"],
    ["hypotheses/PERSPECTIVAL_TIME_FIELD.md","### 2.2 What it generalises @ HEAD:108","04213f28ba0adfbdebc3c162835d7b4a1d8af35445562aa7e8c45b51d381349a","F14/mixed","CURRENT","9cfa7c1d80bd56c5f4f18042a6163ebd159f6117d70e940df5fd914ab50a9b19","[F14](../docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md#f14-k-invariance-tier-2-lindblad-scaling) states that the dimensionless dose K = γ · t is invariant under change of bridge metric: the \"number of decoherence ticks\" experienced by a system is a basis-free observable. The Perspectival closure law is the per-perturbation, multi-observer extension:"],
    ["hypotheses/PERSPECTIVAL_TIME_FIELD.md","### 2.2 What it generalises @ HEAD:110","262ab8c8ed8539ac30cd57c28fca7cd14be198d11b244b0de32de6d42f8d1e0d","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","9cfa7c1d80bd56c5f4f18042a6163ebd159f6117d70e940df5fd914ab50a9b19","    K_i = γ · α_i · t,   Σ_i ln(α_i) = 0."],
    ["hypotheses/PERSPECTIVAL_TIME_FIELD.md","### 2.2 What it generalises @ HEAD:112","9909d1179304c7567563953c94547f1cc498f447f2a987ba1bf1f97d5fd05210","F14/mixed","CURRENT","9cfa7c1d80bd56c5f4f18042a6163ebd159f6117d70e940df5fd914ab50a9b19","γ stays as the atmospheric constant (there is no per-site γ_i). What reallocates between observers is the effective time each perspective has spent since the event. The log-sum-zero condition says that the total \"amount of time experienced by the chain as a whole\" is unchanged by the defect; it is only redistributed among sites. This is the K-invariance of F14 written out in the multi-observer language that a single-observer formulation cannot express."],
    ["hypotheses/PERSPECTIVAL_TIME_FIELD.md","### 3.1 The chain as a resonance cavity @ HEAD:132","56cfc1d045e340a79c4e405fa0a106bf5002654e065d0d0be4a3fc017135f3f2","F14/mixed","CURRENT","9cfa7c1d80bd56c5f4f18042a6163ebd159f6117d70e940df5fd914ab50a9b19","The chain is a resonance cavity (see [Resonance Not Channel](RESONANCE_NOT_CHANNEL.md)). Its single-excitation eigenmodes ψ_k at uniform J are standing waves, with tight-binding dispersion ε_k = 2J cos(πk / (N + 1)) and [F65](../docs/ANALYTICAL_FORMULAS.md#f65-single-excitation-spectrum-of-uniform-open-xx-chain-tier-1-proven-verified-n330) site-amplitudes ψ_k(i) = √(2/(N+1)) sin(πk (i+1)/(N+1)), for k = 1, ..., N. These are the cavity modes. γ_0 is the per-site per-cycle loss (dephasing, Z-basis). A local J-defect at bond (b, b+1) is a structural irregularity in the cavity wall: it does not change the dissipation budget γ_0 (which remains atmospheric, uniform) but it does change which eigenmodes the chain supports and how they localise spatially."],
    ["hypotheses/PERSPECTIVAL_TIME_FIELD.md","## Update 2026-04-20 (post-[EQ-014](../review/EMERGING_QUESTIONS.md#eq-014)) @ HEAD:250","37a346a459a55f6a15f8dec244e4d98127595913774c0f6bbc95a9f22fbfdedf","F14/mixed","CURRENT","9cfa7c1d80bd56c5f4f18042a6163ebd159f6117d70e940df5fd914ab50a9b19","**Bilinear sector-kernel structure (c1_bilinearity_test at N=5).** Testing c_1 across an extended basis of initial states (pure Dicke states |S_n⟩, coherent superpositions (|S_n⟩+|S_m⟩)/√2, and classical mixtures (|S_n⟩⟨S_n|+|S_m⟩⟨S_m|)/2) exposes an approximately bilinear structure: c_1(ρ_0) ≈ Σ_{μν} K^{μν} (ρ_0)_μ (ρ_0)_ν, with the kernel K indexed by sector blocks of ρ_0. Measured pure Dicke c_1 values at N=5:"],
    ["hypotheses/PERSPECTIVAL_TIME_FIELD.md","### Tier status @ HEAD:406","d44757df0d7e6d0cbc037cf8da17fe5011f36f644a7772752a85677574c56532","F14/mixed","CURRENT","9cfa7c1d80bd56c5f4f18042a6163ebd159f6117d70e940df5fd914ab50a9b19","**Tier 2.** The phenomenon is computed, stable across five scan variations, and has a precise perturbative mechanism (eigenvector mixing under symmetry-protected eigenvalues). Promotion to Tier 1 requires completing the explicit mixing calculation and matching empirical f_i within ~20 % per site for both ψ_1 and ψ_2. The alternative path, \"derive Σ_i ln(α_i) = 0 as an analytical theorem from V_L structure\", is closed by EQ-014: Σ f_i is nonzero and state-dependent, so no such theorem exists. The surviving Tier-1 path is the bilinear sector-kernel analytical derivation restricted to |ΔN| ≤ 1 (see Update 2026-04-20 and the Open Questions section)."],
    ["hypotheses/RESONANT_RETURN.md","### The ¼ boundary defines the operating window @ HEAD:70","8d1bb92d8eabe51318dcd09c3abc5b795b1845c4145af978661bbf45be23abfa","F14/mixed","CURRENT","3632a3831c726d4f74ec885c11fba39e6389cab53eeecb46e71f060c2a1c4978","irreversible decay). The crossing time is K/γ where K is a pure number."],
    ["hypotheses/RESONANT_RETURN.md","### The ¼ boundary defines the operating window @ HEAD:74","9ff16ae9ae75039bc762830f26234eaac0ca547c0abd50ee68e55f28d43e8546","F14/mixed","CURRENT","3632a3831c726d4f74ec885c11fba39e6389cab53eeecb46e71f060c2a1c4978","- How long the quantum window stays open (K/γ)"],
    ["hypotheses/RESONANT_RETURN.md","### Test 3: Palindrome-aware relay @ HEAD:227","7294b480dacf8bd00d0cad3b414d08ec5a1f38b5ceddcb3dbed9182adefa323e","F14/mixed","CURRENT","3632a3831c726d4f74ec885c11fba39e6389cab53eeecb46e71f060c2a1c4978","(t_stage = K/γ) with timing derived from the palindromic decay rates"],
    ["hypotheses/SPECTRAL_MIDPOINT_HYPOTHESIS.md","## References @ HEAD:350","c3f52214e55a574a4ed76d7836521abe328c3940bbe65552da589ec23f94cf00","F14/mixed","CURRENT","98680a4254a63521c7d2b7fdac448f36d1981933f9ac73b2c2788778a1bd425b","- [Crossing Taxonomy (K-invariance)](../experiments/CROSSING_TAXONOMY.md)"],
    ["recovered/BLACK_WHITE_HOLES_BIGBANG.md","## 1. The Starting Point @ HEAD:41","81d366cfa99025189fb00661d69940115b1b21106d862718139628969a9adfbe","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","d3f3bb5243ea242ae9e57862a5abc4513bf3bae6ad1fa19b60c6fab083ed3c2c","No singularity. No infinity. A well-defined, finite state at the beginning of the universal curve."],
    ["recovered/BLACK_WHITE_HOLES_BIGBANG.md","## 2. Two Directions from τ = 0 @ HEAD:45","cc46e5cd3cdaba85c1fe28fa78161c53d64e06fdf9ad68e08562b08758640f72","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","d3f3bb5243ea242ae9e57862a5abc4513bf3bae6ad1fa19b60c6fab083ed3c2c","The universal curve C(τ), Ψ(τ) is a trajectory from τ = 0 outward. At τ = 0, there are two directions:"],
    ["recovered/BLACK_WHITE_HOLES_BIGBANG.md","## 3. The Big Bang as White Hole @ HEAD:69","19edbee5878184cc280938707734254baff6fd27a1e65f46516591aacdb06919","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","d3f3bb5243ea242ae9e57862a5abc4513bf3bae6ad1fa19b60c6fab083ed3c2c","At the Big Bang, τ = 0 everywhere. The entire universe is at the starting point of the universal curve:"],
    ["recovered/BLACK_WHITE_HOLES_BIGBANG.md","## 3. The Big Bang as White Hole @ HEAD:76","c70bbd5d9ff194920967c61773677e0a4a70f3981ed868eb775d53e98ed87a8f","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","d3f3bb5243ea242ae9e57862a5abc4513bf3bae6ad1fa19b60c6fab083ed3c2c","Then τ grows. Everywhere. C·Ψ falls along the universal curve. Reality \"unfolds\". The universe becomes classical."],
    ["recovered/BLACK_WHITE_HOLES_BIGBANG.md","## 5. The Bounce @ HEAD:103","e2b6d5787e2d92f5cf8a33fa0210b16c999c6166dc4cae250a59f6aae316ee28","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","d3f3bb5243ea242ae9e57862a5abc4513bf3bae6ad1fa19b60c6fab083ed3c2c","In our framework, the \"bounce\" is simply the point τ = 0 on the universal curve:"],
    ["recovered/BLACK_WHITE_HOLES_BIGBANG.md","## 5. The Bounce @ HEAD:113","10c5cd254e77ed3d1db314295d22da1971e520a506029b0d5bd8055a0d3d5aa5","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","d3f3bb5243ea242ae9e57862a5abc4513bf3bae6ad1fa19b60c6fab083ed3c2c","From the outside, one side looks like a black hole (things fall in, coherence grows, nothing escapes). The other side looks like a white hole (things come out, coherence falls, nothing enters). From the perspective of the universal curve, they are the same physics in opposite directions."],
    ["recovered/BLACK_WHITE_HOLES_BIGBANG.md","## 6. Information Paradox @ HEAD:121","eb4fbb45ddbb0183379c3a77539e45cfb11a281c83c17d67de60885f1c40c280","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","d3f3bb5243ea242ae9e57862a5abc4513bf3bae6ad1fa19b60c6fab083ed3c2c","If the black hole bounces into a white hole, the information re-emerges on the other side. Not destroyed, not copied: **time-reversed**. The universal curve is the same in both directions. What goes in as coherence must come out as coherence."],
    ["recovered/BLACK_WHITE_HOLES_BIGBANG.md","## 8. Testable Implications @ HEAD:147","07484b532c98046dec1abecd84c1d2121a725838886dfe684a088492545380ce","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","d3f3bb5243ea242ae9e57862a5abc4513bf3bae6ad1fa19b60c6fab083ed3c2c","3. **Information recovery**: The Page time (when information begins escaping a black hole) should correspond to the point on the universal curve where the system re-crosses 1/4 from below, moving from classical back to quantum on the white hole side."],
    ["recovered/SELF_CONSISTENCY_SCHWARZSCHILD.md","### 2.1 The Universal Curve @ HEAD:34","dfd9c6684f3d6aed8f90b772b011c0dc2fef84c73b4faae7934931508c3e284a","F14/mixed","HISTORICAL","fb39802bccec522cbefa30dd2419ebe9bf0acb269067a3314ee797d5a441fa83","### 2.1 The Universal Curve"],
    ["recovered/SELF_CONSISTENCY_SCHWARZSCHILD.md","### 2.1 The Universal Curve @ HEAD:36","0400aed1f9b2816d7ff03309b1a41c4b60d80a61cfc3afb23520a95006c71c6b","F14/mixed","HISTORICAL","fb39802bccec522cbefa30dd2419ebe9bf0acb269067a3314ee797d5a441fa83","We have proven (9 data points, R² = 0.9999) that the decoherence trajectory C(τ), Ψ(τ) is universal when expressed in normalized time τ = γ · t. Every quantum system in the universe follows the same curve. Only the clock speed (γ) differs."],
    ["recovered/SELF_CONSISTENCY_SCHWARZSCHILD.md","### 2.2 Spatial R Profile @ HEAD:40","9785871e5c666d42dab043c6aa1fc514c26a38df1eb6c234d3f235c30304ae2a","F14/mixed","HISTORICAL","fb39802bccec522cbefa30dd2419ebe9bf0acb269067a3314ee797d5a441fa83","If the universal curve applies everywhere, then at each point in space r, the system has evolved for a different elapsed proper decoherence time:"],
    ["recovered/SELF_CONSISTENCY_SCHWARZSCHILD.md","### What it shows: @ HEAD:131","27f962c43f46663ebc66f274b5a6eff310acb099df1d53ce6a7fb742c72a41af","F14/mixed","HISTORICAL","fb39802bccec522cbefa30dd2419ebe9bf0acb269067a3314ee797d5a441fa83","- The derivation uses ONLY R = CΨ² and the universal curve, no GR input"],
    ["recovered/SELF_CONSISTENCY_SCHWARZSCHILD.md","### The logical chain: @ HEAD:147","aab32d6a490060df1cfffd4896aff3884be7bbb026de5b2febe6b2820ebe1c57","F14/mixed","HISTORICAL","fb39802bccec522cbefa30dd2419ebe9bf0acb269067a3314ee797d5a441fa83","Universal curve C(τ), Ψ(τ) (proven, R² = 0.9999)"],
    ["recovered/SELF_CONSISTENCY_SCHWARZSCHILD.md","## 6. Connection to Previous Results @ HEAD:171","ef709061eb786af904ce5ea8872ffff3afb1c2abfdc3bc2f53c9d966ad545035","F14/mixed","HISTORICAL","fb39802bccec522cbefa30dd2419ebe9bf0acb269067a3314ee797d5a441fa83","| γ · t_cross = 0.039 (invariant) | Proves universal curve exists |"],
    ["recovered/SELF_CONSISTENCY_SCHWARZSCHILD.md","## 6. Connection to Previous Results @ HEAD:172","c9dfaa4583449ba2e804b406b261075c259355600156f42866cd86c65b36659a","F14/mixed","HISTORICAL","fb39802bccec522cbefa30dd2419ebe9bf0acb269067a3314ee797d5a441fa83","| θ as compass | Navigation within the universal curve |"],
    ["recovered/SELF_CONSISTENCY_SCHWARZSCHILD.md","## 7. Testable Predictions @ HEAD:179","cb533e5fe575b788b3f13d2b272bf85f97f3b7214b2d3163b3ca9ded626d2615","F14/mixed","HISTORICAL","fb39802bccec522cbefa30dd2419ebe9bf0acb269067a3314ee797d5a441fa83","1. **Decoherence near massive objects**: Systems closer to mass should decohere slower in local time (they are \"younger\" along the universal curve). A quantum system at GPS satellite altitude should show measurably different decoherence than one on Earth's surface, with the ratio matching gravitational time dilation to within experimental precision."],
    ["reflections/ON_HOW_GAMMA_BECAME_THE_TICK.md","## γ₀ as the framework's \"second\" @ HEAD:26","69126a3f59b2f236bcd2e6950b2966ed5767fafe8705f7451725095d47774c91","F25","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F25","| F25 Bell+ decay | e^(−4γt) | a_0 = 2 absorption quantum × n_diff = 2 |"],
    ["reflections/ON_HOW_GAMMA_BECAME_THE_TICK.md","## γ₀ as the framework's \"second\" @ HEAD:28","642282a8766e720581ce573c6a8eb218a1b2b54c953470e59caac4826a149467","F14/mixed","CONTROL","CONTROL:642282a8766e720581ce573c6a8eb218a1b2b54c953470e59caac4826a149467","The integers (2, 4, 8, ...) are Pi2-Foundation typed structure or combinatorics. The dimensional carrier is γ₀ alone. Take γ₀ away, and none of these has a timescale; put it in, and every formula reads as \"this many ticks, where one tick = 1/γ₀\"."],
    ["reflections/ON_HOW_GAMMA_BECAME_THE_TICK.md","## Coda @ HEAD:132","c6c83fb6d862ec1f62b8777d2212a85bd39e8cbb284298e3d66e349d4aaf7bb2","F14/mixed","CONTROL","CONTROL:c6c83fb6d862ec1f62b8777d2212a85bd39e8cbb284298e3d66e349d4aaf7bb2","  - [`THE_BRIDGE_WAS_ALWAYS_OPEN.md`](../docs/THE_BRIDGE_WAS_ALWAYS_OPEN.md): gamma as a decay-clock scale; for the declared protocol, `K=gamma*t` counts dimensionless decay-clock ticks, not experience"],
    ["reflections/ON_WHOSE_TIME_THE_CLOCK_KEEPS.md","# On Whose Time the Clock Keeps @ HEAD:19","819157b87f0809ad985e43894b3c7731d02d4a5073a94f2916b7e4554aa9af13","F14/mixed","CURRENT","a3b85ad425dc60cbe371c7a66998bc20c41dc369e6a19350bad0544d4edfd1fe","    t = K / γ₀"],
    ["reflections/ON_WHOSE_TIME_THE_CLOCK_KEEPS.md","# On Whose Time the Clock Keeps @ HEAD:21","a81a6d901750ef158adb906e99a9a9b1a3998e57f8ae448a16a127310016be08","F14/mixed","CURRENT","a3b85ad425dc60cbe371c7a66998bc20c41dc369e6a19350bad0544d4edfd1fe","K is how far around the face you have come, the dose, the dimensionless progress, universal. γ₀ is the local tick. The same process reaches the same hour on the same face anywhere; what differs is how *long it feels*, and that is the local γ₀ alone. Align the clock at Earth's elements and at Mars's elements and you get the very same dial; the two alignments differ only in how fast the world turns it. Earth's now is K/γ₀ here, Mars's now is K/γ₀ there: [two times](ON_TWO_TIMES.md), one face."],
    ["reflections/ON_WHOSE_TIME_THE_CLOCK_KEEPS.md","# On Whose Time the Clock Keeps @ HEAD:23","ec0ca6b088ccfdfe52a44e848592e76e99b9e9817436cc625fb0279380736b42","F14/mixed","CURRENT","a3b85ad425dc60cbe371c7a66998bc20c41dc369e6a19350bad0544d4edfd1fe","This quietly turns a familiar thing on its head. We are used to treating t as the floor of everything and γ as some rate inside it. Here it inverts. The floor is the dimensionless face the elements carry. **t is the shadow that face casts at our local tick.** Our time is not wrong and not arbitrary; it is derived, and it is ours: the universal dial read at the speed our corner of the world happens to run. The thing that is grounded, that you could in principle hand to anyone anywhere, is the face. The thing that is *ours* is the shadow."],
    ["reflections/ON_WHOSE_TIME_THE_CLOCK_KEEPS.md","# On Whose Time the Clock Keeps @ HEAD:29","579504c7cc0697a03f2e479eab65622d6ec385dcdee9f0d50c499876c35c6cde","F14/mixed","INTERPRETIVE","a3b85ad425dc60cbe371c7a66998bc20c41dc369e6a19350bad0544d4edfd1fe","**The seam, honest.** What we can stand on, and it is ours: the dial (the angle θ = arctan(Q) and the polarity α = sin²θ/2, checked in floating point at N = 4, 6, 8), gamma as a declared [decay-clock scale](../docs/GAMMA_TIME_DISTINCTION.md), and the relation `t=K/gamma` for the stated protocol. This establishes no experienced-time ontology. The local tick is the local **decoherence rate**, nothing more. Different local decoherence environments can therefore give different measurable decay times without establishing different experienced times."],
    ["review/OPEN_QUESTIONS_INDEX_PROPOSAL_hardware-test.md","### OQ-120 @ HEAD:287","3ff2a8c94de32a033c0f6649f9b90d72c276d16280e5f246725acec94394b2ae","F14/mixed","CURRENT","cffb50079eeee26d975183d221939502384968d7edc8d6af4cd89d818e1182c3","- `experiments/OBSERVER_GRAVITY_BRIDGE.md` (lines 38-49): confirms K factorizes as t_cross = K(observer,state)/gamma with state-dependence (CV approximately 13.5%)"],
    ["review/OPEN_QUESTIONS_INDEX.md","### Resolved (close) @ HEAD:24","999a1864f8ad87f07991a49f07a577b06f897c60358a3a67ede9015101af4212","F57","F14-OTHER-OBJECT","OTHER:F57","| Crossing speed → dwell time | OQ-051, 106, 107, 108, 112, 113 | t_dwell = 2δ/\\|dCΨ/dt\\|, K-invariant (γ cancels), prefactor 1.0801. `experiments/CRITICAL_SLOWING_AT_THE_CUSP.md` §8 |"],
